<title>USA: Jacor, American Radio swap stations.</title>
<headline>Jacor, American Radio swap stations.</headline>
<dateline>COVINGTON, Ky. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jacor Communications Inc said Thursday it will swap its four Kansas radio stations to American Radio Systems Corp for six Ohio stations in a cashless transaction.</p>
<p>Jacor will add the Dayton, Ohio, stations of WMMX-FM, WTUE-FM, WLQT-FM, WXEG-FM, WBTT-FM and WONE-AM, while American radio takes over WDAF-AM, KYYS-FM, KMXV-FM and KUDL-FM in Kansas City.</p>
<p>Jacor's stock traded at 36-7/8 in the late afternoon today, down 1/8. American Radio traded at 39-1/4, up 1/4.</p>
